  "dct_description_sm": [
    "Relief shown pictorially.; Printed from a new plate made by Mortier for the fourth volume of his 'Nouveau Theatre de l'Italie,' an expanded reprint of Blaeu's 'Theatrum Civitatum Italiae.'--Koeman (pages 332, 356).; Upper image, upper right, plate number: LV.; Upper image includes index labels for Batterie des Turcs, Fort St. Lean and Fort Degenveld.; View of Šibenik beseiged by the Ottomans in 1645, showing fortresses and fortifications, skirmishes, castles, churches and buildings, ships, hills and vegetation; Plan of Šibenik emphasizing walls and fortifications.; View of Šibenik and the port of Šibenik from the Gulf of Venice.",
